compat/libucl is NOT distributed under goucl's licence
======================================================

The BSD 2-clause LICENSE at the root of this repository covers the goucl
module. It does not cover this module, and must not be read as covering it.
This module is distributed under whatever terms the original library is
under — which is to say: none are stated, by anyone.


Why there are no terms to state
-------------------------------

Four files here come from github.com/mitchellh/go-libucl, which states no
licence at all: no LICENSE file, no per-file copyright headers, and no
statement in its README. The repository is archived on GitHub with no
instruction about reuse, and a request to its author asking for clarification
went unanswered.

    decoder.go ........ Mitchell Hashimoto, byte-identical to upstream
    object_test.go .... Mitchell Hashimoto, byte-identical to upstream
    parser_test.go .... Mitchell Hashimoto, byte-identical to upstream
    decoder_test.go ... Mitchell Hashimoto, differing only by the markers
                        that disable one test which is broken upstream

No licence stated means all rights reserved by default. Attribution is credit,
not permission, and nothing in this repository can grant what its author has
not granted.

compat.go and decoder_flaky_test.go are this project's own work and carry no
such encumbrance. They are also useless on their own: decoder.go is the file
that does the decoding.


What this means if you depend on this module
--------------------------------------------

Redistributing this module means redistributing those four files under terms
nobody has granted. That is a decision to make deliberately, before depending
on it, rather than one to discover later.

The module is kept separate from the rest of goucl precisely so that this
decision is yours to make and nobody makes it by accident: programs that use
only the idiomatic API never receive these files, because they are not in that
module and nothing in it depends on them.


The way out
-----------

This module exists to get a working program off the C toolchain without a
rewrite. It is a migration step, not a destination.

The github.com/derekmarcotte/goucl module carries none of these files, is
original work over a translation of libucl, and is distributed under the
BSD 2-clause terms in the root LICENSE. Moving onto it removes the question
entirely. USAGE.md works the conversion through end to end, with the API
mapping and the one behavioural difference that matters.

See the NOTICE file at the repository root for full provenance of everything
in this repository.
